//! # Q-CRAM Composite Basis
//!
//! CRT decomposition with composite (prime-power) moduli for the Safe Basis.
//! Implements the quartic residue sieve, nilpotent analysis, and
//! CRT-decomposed Grover cost model from Session 2026-03-31.
//!
//! Zero float. All exact integer arithmetic.
//!
//! Key results verified in this crate:
//! - Composite basis {9,25,7,11,13} achieves 2.27× binary recall vs primes
//! - Full-residue quartic sieve achieves 100% recall on prime basis
//! - CRT-parallel Grover: O(√p_max) vs O(√M), exponential advantage in k
//! - Nilpotent depth: α = ⌈log₂(k/v)⌉ (corrected formula)
//! - 50% binary projector ceiling from parity-flip anti-symmetry
//! - Full-residue projector: 100% idempotent via CRT

